<Layout title="Drylining Livingston | Partition Walls &amp; Ceilings Contractors" description="Professional drylining contractors in Livingston. Expert partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation for Livingston town centre, Livingston Rural, and the wider EH postcode region. Free quotes." canonical="/areas/livingston/" schema={schema}>
  <section style="position:relative;min-height:400px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1a1a2e 0%,#16213e 100%);overflow:hidden;"> <img src="/images/hero-main.jpg" alt="Drylining services in Livingston and West Lothian" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;opacity:0.25;"> <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;text-align:center;padding:60px 20px;"> <nav style="font-size:13px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);margin-bottom:12px;"> <a href="/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Home</a> / <a href="/areas/" style="text-decoration:none;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.70);">Areas</a> / <span style="color:#ffffff;">Drylining in Livingston</span> </nav> <h1 style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px);font-weight:800;color:#ffffff;margin-bottom:14px;line-height:1.15;">Drylining in Livingston</h1> <p style="font-size:17px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.6;">CSCS-accredited drylining contractors delivering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard across Livingston town centre, Livingston Rural, and the wider West Lothian area.</p> </div> </section> <section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;"> <div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);"> <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Drylining Livingston provides drylining, partition walls, and suspended ceilings across Livingston (EH54), Livingston Rural, and the wider West Lothian area. Experienced with new build developments, retail park fit-outs, and commercial refurbishments in Livingston's growing town centre.</p> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Drylining Services in Livingston</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Livingston is West Lothian's largest town with a population of over 56,000 people in the EH54 postcode area. As one of Scotland's designated new towns, Livingston has undergone significant growth since the 1960s, with major retail, commercial, and residential developments throughout the town centre and surrounding areas. This diversity means our drylining contractors work on everything from new build residential developments to large-scale commercial fit-outs at the Meadowbank Retail Park and Almond Valley Business Park.</p> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The town's ongoing regeneration projects — including the Meadowbank expansion, the Almond Valley business park developments, and new residential schemes in Livingston Rural — create consistent demand for commercial drylining services. We deliver partition wall installation, suspended ceilings, and fire-rated wall systems for office refurbishments, retail units, healthcare premises, and educational buildings throughout the EH54 postcode area. All work is carried out to Scottish Building Standards Part H and Part T standards.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What We Do in Livingston</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our Livingston crew handles everything from single-room domestic renovations on High Street to large-scale commercial fit-outs at Meadowbank Retail Park — covering partition walls, suspended ceilings, and plasterboard installation across the entire EH54 postcode region.</p> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><strong>New build handover drylining</strong> — Pre-completion drylining for housing developments in Livingston, Livingston Rural, and the surrounding West Lothian areas</li> <li><strong>Commercial fit-outs</strong> — Office refurbs, retail units, and restaurant conversions along the town centre, Meadowbank Retail Park, and Almond Valley Business Park</li> <li><strong>Fire-rated walls</strong> — Multi-storey residential and commercial buildings require Scottish Building Standards compliance, delivered with full documentation for West Lothian Council building standards</li> <li><strong>Suspended ceilings</strong> — Office refurbs, healthcare premises, and education facilities throughout the Livingston area</li> <li><strong>Acoustic partitions</strong> — Residential blocks and hotel conversions near Livingston Town Centre and the Almond Valley</li> <li><strong>Period property drylining</strong> — Internal wall insulation, room conversions, and partition walls in historic properties around Livingston and West Lothian</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Areas of Livingston We Cover</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li>Livingston town centre and High Street (EH54)</li> <li>Meadowbank Retail Park (EH54)</li> <li>Almond Valley Business Park (EH54)</li> <li>Livingston Rural and Broxburn Road (EH54)</li> <li>East Kilbride Road and Livingston Village (EH54)</li> <li>Barrhall and East Calder (EH54)</li> <li>Dechmont and Fauldhouse (EH54)</li> <li>Longridge and Whitburn (EH54)</li> <li>Rosewell and West Linton (EH54)</li> <li>Mid Calder and Winchburgh (EH54)</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Livingston Building Standards &amp; Planning</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Livingston falls under <strong>West Lothian Council</strong> for building standards and planning. The town has numerous modern developments alongside older historic properties, particularly in the town centre and surrounding villages. Many properties are within local conservation areas, meaning any internal structural alterations or external drylining insulation may require planning permission. We work closely with clients, architects, and the council building standards surveyors to ensure every project — from a simple room partition in a Victorian terrace to a large commercial fit-out at Meadowbank Retail Park — is fully compliant with current Scottish Building Standards.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Us for Livingston Projects</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">As a Livingston-based drylining team with daily operations across West Lothian, we understand the area's unique demands. From easy motorway access via the M8 and M9 to working around the town's growing commercial developments, our crew knows the area inside out. All operatives are DBS checked, fully uniformed, and experienced in delivering quality work in Livingston's mix of new build and period properties.</p> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Related Services</h2> <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <a href="/services/partition-walls/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Partition Walls</a> <a href="/services/fire-rated-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Fire-Rated Drylining</a> <a href="/services/acoustic-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Acoustic Drylining</a> <a href="/services/refurbishment-drylining/" style="text-decoration:none;padding:10px 14px;background:var(--white);border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);">Refurbishment Drylining</a> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Nearby Areas</h2> <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;"> <li><a href="/areas/edinburgh/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Edinburgh</a> — 25 minutes via M8</li> <li><a href="/areas/falkirk/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Falkirk</a> — 20 minutes via M9</li> <li><a href="/areas/musselburgh/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Musselburgh</a> — 35 minutes via M8</li> <li><a href="/areas/dalkeith/" style="color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Dalkeith</a> — 30 minutes via M8</li> </ul> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2> <div style="margin-bottom:2rem;"> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> What is dry lining and how does it work? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Dry lining is a method of finishing internal walls and ceilings with plasterboard rather than applying several layers of wet plaster. The boards can be fixed directly to brick or blockwork with drywall adhesive, often called the dot and dab method, or screwed to a timber or metal frame. Once the plasterboard is secure, the joints and screw heads are covered with tape and jointing compound. The surface can then be sanded, painted, wallpapered or finished with a thin plaster skim. Dry lining is commonly used in new builds, extensions, renovations and commercial properties. It provides a smooth finish quickly and can also create space for insulation, soundproofing materials, electrical cables and pipework. </div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> Do I need planning permission for drylining in Livingston? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Internal drylining usually falls under permitted development rights and doesn't require planning permission. However, if your property is listed or within a Conservation Area in Livingston or West Lothian, you'll need listed building consent for any internal alterations. We advise checking with West Lothian Council's planning department before starting work on period properties.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> What are Scottish Building Standards for drylining? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Scottish Building Standards Part H covers heat and energy efficiency, Part T covers ventilation, and Part C covers structural adequacy. All our drylining work in Livingston complies with current Scottish Building Standards. For fire-rated walls, we follow the Fire Standard (Part B) and provide full documentation. We also ensure thermal insulation meets the latest Part H requirements, which is particularly important for new build developments in Livingston.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> How long does drylining take in Livingston? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> A typical single-room drylining job takes 2–3 days for framing and board installation, plus 1–2 days for taping, jointing, and sanding. Larger commercial projects at Meadowbank Retail Park or Almond Valley Business Park can take 1–4 weeks depending on scale. We work efficiently to minimise disruption, especially on new build handovers where tight deadlines are common.</div> </details> </div> <div style="border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:1rem;"> <details style="border:none;"> <summary style="width:100%;text-align:left;background:var(--white);border:none;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;font-size:1rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--secondary);cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;list-style:none;"> Do you offer free quotes for Livingston projects? <span style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--primary);">+</span> </summary> <div style="padding:0 1.5rem;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.7;font-size:0.9375rem;"> Yes, we offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Livingston and West Lothian. We'll assess your property, discuss your requirements, and provide a detailed written quote within 48 hours. Call us on 0800 820 3090 or fill in our contact form to arrange your free site visit.</div> </details> </div> </div> <h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Get a Free Livingston Quote</h2> <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2rem;">We offer free, no-obligation site visits and written quotes for all drylining projects across Livingston. Call us or fill in our quick form.</p> <div style="margin-top:2rem;text-align:center;"> <a href="/get-quote/" class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;">Get a Free Livingston Quote</a> <a href="tel:08008203090" class="btn btn-secondary" style="font-size:1.0625rem;padding:1rem 2.5rem;border:2px solid var(--primary);background:transparent;color:var(--primary);margin-left:0.5rem;">FREEPHONE 0800 820 3090</a> </div> </div></section>
</Layout>
